{
  "_help": [
    "Frame ref: 'row:col' on the sheet, 'row:a-b' for a range, '@name:i' = frame i of a generated recipe, trailing '~' = mirrored.",
    "Names ending in _L / _dL / _uL (left, down-left, up-left) get an automatic _R / _dR / _uR twin (mirrored frames, dx negated) unless the twin is defined here.",
    "Directions: L, dL, F (down, towards you), dR, R, uR, B (up, away), uL. stand_<dir> poses form a ring, so turning goes through the neighbours.",
    "generated: frames made in code from sheet frames. ops: squash [row, k] deletes k rows (body drops), erase [x0, y0, x1, y1], shift [dx, dy], paint [x, y | ['top', dy], rows, {char: [ref, x, y]}] where each char takes the color of that sheet pixel and '-' clears. `pet.py gen` writes them to assets/generated/.",
    "poses: still key frames = nodes of the graph. links: [poseA, poseB, ms] two-way edges; ms = how long the next pose is shown.",
    "clips: animations that start and end in a pose. ms / dx / dy: one number or one per frame; dx, dy = sprite px moved per frame (dy > 0 is up the screen). cycle: the pose stands in for the last frame (walk loops).",
    "Steps (behaviour, on_click, on_drop, scroll.edge): play: clip (times = [min,max]), go: pose (path via links), hold: [min_s,max_s], pose: jump straight to a pose, roam: [min_px,max_px] walk to a random spot (run = chance to run).",
    "behaviour: per pose, the cat's small habits as weighted steps (w). The mind decides what to do; these fill the time in between.",
    "on_click: per pose, list of alternative step sequences ('default' for the rest). on_drop: steps after being dragged and released.",
    "scroll: scrolling the window the cat stands on carries the cat with the content. Pushed against the window edge it hangs on (held frame), then plays edge. Scrolled more than wake_after pt in one go, it reacts as if clicked. top_inset: title bar height, pt. line_pt: pt per line for non-trackpad wheels.",
    "mind: needs (0..1) change per minute by activity; see brain/mind.py for how they pick the next activity."
  ],
